# Normalise line endings in the working tree to LF on every platform.
#
# Every file is stored LF in the index, but without this git applies its
# platform default on checkout — CRLF on the Windows runner — and `gofmt` reads
# a CRLF Go file as unformatted. That made the "Check formatting" step fail on
# all 66 files in the repository, on every run, including the first one on
# main: the step had been red since CI was introduced and nothing noticed
# because nothing gated on it.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` fixes the checkout rather than the check, so the answer is
# the real repository rather than a gofmt invocation that ignores CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The scripts the release and the container build copy verbatim. A CRLF shell
# script in a Docker RUN fails with a confusing "/bin/sh^M: not found".
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf